    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "MotionGraph runtime-data generation (phase-2 downsink of the stylecut consumer\r\norchestration).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  build-runtime-manifest                Orchestrate MG runtime data strictly from the package\r\n                                        runtime_data_acquisition_recipe.\r\n  track-subject-mask                    Atomic: subject mask/VOS. Uses draft-aware mask_tracking_matting\r\n                                        when --ref + --seg-id or an active editor session is available;\r\n                                        otherwise falls back to media object-matting-track with --input.\r\n  encode-subject-alpha                  Atomic: encode mask frames into subject_alpha.v1 (RLE) +\r\n                                        subject_transform.v1 (draft_us, 0-based).\r\n  track-plane-quad                      Atomic: plane seed + in-memory video-tracking into plane_quad.v1\r\n                                        (persist_to_file=false, no draft copy).\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track-subject-mask / encode-subject-alpha / track-plane-quad are the atomic steps it dispatches; they can also be called directly.\r\n\r\nNOTE\r\n  Produces subject_alpha.v1 / subject_transform.v1 / plane_quad.v1 with time_base=draft_us (frame time_us rebased to 0). Apply via `draft effect add --type motiongraph --runtime-data-manifest <manifest>`.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "MotionGraph runtime-data generation (phase-2 downsink of the stylecut consumer\r\norchestration).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  build-runtime-manifest                Orchestrate MG runtime data strictly from the package\r\n                                        runtime_data_acquisition_recipe.\r\n  track-subject-mask                    Atomic: subject mask/VOS. Uses draft-aware mask_tracking_matting\r\n                                        when --ref + --seg-id or an active editor session is available;\r\n                                        otherwise falls back to media object-matting-track with --input.\r\n  encode-subject-alpha                  Atomic: encode mask frames into subject_alpha.v1 (RLE) +\r\n                                        subject_transform.v1 (draft_us, 0-based).\r\n  track-plane-quad                      Atomic: plane seed + in-memory video-tracking into plane_quad.v1\r\n                                        (persist_to_file=false, no draft copy).\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track